  "description": "WEGLAY crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C60 H96 Eu8 Ge12 N4 O64,2(C12 H8 N2),16(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu1A (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu2A (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu3A (Eu) has 8 O neighbors; Eu4A (Eu) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 3 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.831-3.855 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 109.86-110.74°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C84H144Eu8Ge12N8O80. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 24 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 16 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
